@startuml ownership
 title Civ13 retained-reference ownership after GC repairs
 class Datum {
   gcDestroyed : legacy timestamp
   gc_destroyed : modern lifecycle state
   Destroy()
   finalize_qdel()
 }
 class Atom
 Datum <|-- Atom
 class Callproc {
   queue : pending helpers
   helpers : at most 5000 cleared helpers
   by_object : pending targets only
   release_helper()
   unqueue(target)
 }
 class Helper {
   target
   arguments
   deadline
   index_target
 }
 class GlobalPool {
   explicit reviewed type families
   at most 100 per type / 1000 total
   idle expiry : 5 minutes
   retire at most 32 per GC run
 }
 class Garbage {
   destroyed : text ref -> timestamp
   hard_references : HARDDEL hints only
   300 checks / 30 forced deletes
   timestamp identity guard
 }
 class ProcessSnapshot {
   retain on budgeted yield
   release after complete run
 }
 class NanoUI {
   master
   children
   close()
 }
 class WeakHandle {
   text reference
   resolve()
 }
 class Reagents {
   owner backlink
   cleanup()
 }
 Callproc o-- Helper
 Helper --> Datum : pending target / args
 GlobalPool o-- Datum : retired reusable objects
 Garbage ..> Atom : ordinary queue stores text refs
 Garbage --> Datum : explicit forced ownership
 ProcessSnapshot --> Datum : active or yielded pass only
 NanoUI o-- NanoUI : detach independently closed children
 WeakHandle ..> Datum : never owns or deletes target
 Atom o-- Reagents
 Reagents --> Atom : cleared on retirement
 note bottom
 Source-level ownership, not heap byte sizes.
 Runtime reclamation and production latency require observation.
 end note
@enduml

@startuml retirement
 title Retirement and bounded reuse
 [*] --> Active : construction
 Active --> Cleaning : qdel / modern reentry guard
 Cleaning --> Active : LETMELIVE
 Cleaning --> Retired : cleanup exactly once / cancel pending callbacks
 Retired --> Pooled : reviewed type within budgets
 Pooled --> Active : remove idle ownership / ResetVars / New
 Pooled --> Queued : idle expiry / bounded sweep
 Retired --> Queued : ordinary atom or HARDDEL
 Retired --> Reclaimable : IWILLGC
 Retired --> Deleted : direct finalizer or HARDDEL_NOW
 Queued --> Reclaimable : all strong owners release
 Queued --> Deleted : timeout / matching timestamp / bounded forced delete
 Reclaimable --> [*] : native reclamation, timing opaque
 Deleted --> [*]
 note right of Pooled
 Sleeping effect routines require their original activation token.
 Old activations cannot move or delete a reused object.
 end note
@enduml
